# Dotfiles

Personal configuration files managed with [Dotbot](https://github.com/anishathalye/dotbot).

## Quick Start (Recommended)

On a new machine, run:

```bash
bash <(curl -s https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gameforce/dotfiles/master/bootstrap.sh)
```

Or the classic way:

```bash
git clone --recursive https://github.com/gameforce/dotfiles.git ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
./bootstrap.sh
```

The bootstrap script will:

- Install required packages (`zsh`, `git`, `vim`, `pipx`, `keychain`, etc.)
- Clone/update this repository
- Install/update Dotbot via `pipx`
- Create the necessary symlinks
- Install the Hack Nerd Font (Mono) used by the p10k prompt
- Set `zsh` as the default shell

After it finishes, log out and log back in (or run `exec zsh`).

## Manual Installation

If you prefer to do it step by step:

```bash
git clone --recursive git@github.com:gameforce/dotfiles.git ~/.dotfiles
cd ~/.dotfiles
pipx install dotbot
dotbot -d ~/.dotfiles -c install.conf.yaml
chsh -s $(which zsh)
```

## Updating

```bash
cd ~/.dotfiles
git pull
./bootstrap.sh
```

## Structure

| Path | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `shell/` | zsh configuration, aliases, functions, environment |
| `git/` | Git configuration |
| `vim/` | Vim configuration |
| `fonts/` | On-demand Nerd Font install scripts (see below, nothing vendored) |
| `bootstrap.sh` | One-command installer |
| `install.conf.yaml` | Dotbot configuration |

## Fonts

No font files are vendored in this repo. `fonts/install-nerd-font.sh`
(Linux/macOS, run automatically by `bootstrap.sh`) and
`fonts/install-nerd-font.ps1` (Windows, run automatically by
`install.ps1`) always download the current **Hack Nerd Font Mono**
release straight from
[ryanoasis/nerd-fonts](https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/latest)
and install it for the current user. Re-run either script any time
to update the font or grab a different one, e.g.:

```bash
fonts/install-nerd-font.sh Meslo
```

```powershell
.\fonts\install-nerd-font.ps1 -FontName Meslo
```

After installing, point your terminal's font at **"Hack Nerd Font Mono"**
(Windows Terminal, ConEmu, iTerm2, GNOME Terminal, etc. all take a regular
installed font name here — no special "Windows compatible" build is
needed, that variant was retired upstream years ago).

## Notes

- Uses **Antigen** + **Powerlevel10k**
- SSH key recommended: `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_github`
- `keychain` is used to manage SSH keys

